So, I was playing a Valk (as decided by !rng @char on #nethack). I had
to kill coaligned unicorn at Sokoban, then I found early wand of
wishing somewhere in the Mines. I zapped for GDSM, only to be
surprised later to learn it is cursed. Of course it was, just like the
two "blessed" scrolls of charging... wishing with negative luck is a
bitch. Anyway, I hoped that this Valk could break my game-time speed
record so I proceeded quickly down. Unfortunately, the speed was quite
underwhelming, but after some time I was ready for the ascension run
and I proceeded as fast as possible, using Asmodeus to retrieve the
amulet. Quite uniquely, apart from the usual skillset, my Valk was a
somewhat capable spellcaster: magic missile at 0% fail, remove curse
at about 30% fail. Anyway, all was rather uneventful until I reached
the Astral Plane. I had some home work to do, so I hoped to pull the
ascension off quickly so I could resume. That was really bad idea. I
went towards the Famine altar with a wished for chickatrice corpse.
After meeting Famine, I zapped magic missile, but it did not kill her.
I wielded my +6 Excalibur, but before I could finish her, I was
fainting from her attacks. My winning game was suddenly in
unrecoverable situation and I only watched as surrounding monsters
were bashing me to my death.

My mistakes:
- burdened -- always a big mistake; I got burdened by the chickatrice
corpse I think
- not satiated on arrival; another elementary issue
- no operable wand of death; I had two death wands, but both empty
from having to kill Rodney too many times; I had wished for magic
marker on the Planes, I should have paused to recharge on of the
wands.
- have potion of full healing in main inventory; stack of !oFH in bag
might be too far away in some situations.

